 ],
 "summary_en": "I found five facts, all about where patients are treated. None of them is a recent lung-cancer-specific decision. Eloisa (South Savo) runs pulmonology clinics in Mikkeli and Savonlinna, which take patients by doctor's referral. Radiotherapy and highly specialised cancer care are done outside the county: KYS in Kuopio covers South Savo for highly specialised care, and Nova in Jyväskylä gives part of South Savo's radiotherapy. Patients from the county have to travel for radiotherapy; in 2022 the local hospital district was working out the cost of its own radiotherapy unit in Mikkeli, but I found nothing on whether that went ahead. I found no county-specific lung cancer pathway, waiting-time figures, nurse navigator, screening pilot or MDT arrangement.",
 "not_found_en": "I searched without result for Eloisa council decisions on lung cancer or on the Mikkeli radiotherapy unit, a local lung cancer pathway, and South Savo lung cancer waiting-time or quality figures; the national registry reports I read give figures only by large region (Eastern Finland), not for South Savo.",
